        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T16:48:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, I was wanting to have the __pkvm_reprivilege_vcpu() as a stand alone function which could probably be used else where if needed and not gated by this constraint(safely for sure). And logic for gating if a hypercall is valid seems to be most appropriate in vmexit.c. But if you think its better to have pkvm_initialized local to init_finalise.c, I could probably have a wrapper function pkvm_handle_reprivilege_hc() check for this and call __pkvm_reprivilege_vcpu(). What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "1d0d9ec1_62c7b00d",
      "revId": "9ba54075d31d7de0c9ed21e82ace895b65984957",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
