      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T19:34:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have much problem with the current code either, my last comment was rather about your suggestion to add pkvm_handle_reprivilege_hc()... Anyway, nevermind, since:\n\n\u003e Regarding the use case, I had one use case to reprivilege when iommu init fails, because we have pkvm_initialized already set by that time.\n\nIndeed, makes sense.\n\nNow it seems to me the nicest way would be to have __pkvm_reprivilege_vcpu() which doesn\u0027t do the check, and pkvm_reprivilege_vcpu() wrapper which does the check. (BTW those double underscores we have in __pkvm_init_finalise() and many other function names are quite pointless, I think.)",
      "parentUuid": "b5052672_9175ac43",
      "revId": "9ba54075d31d7de0c9ed21e82ace895b65984957",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
