      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e\u003e Regarding the use case, I had one use case to reprivilege when iommu init fails, \u003e\u003e because we have pkvm_initialized already set by that time.\n\u003e \n\u003e Indeed, makes sense.\n\nAlthough after more thought, I don\u0027t quite get it: reprivilege is still initiated by the host, via the hypercall, so on pKVM side we\u0027re still gonna validate it in a single place (just the check is gonna be different, e.g. check for iommu initialized instead of pkvm_initialized, or something like that), so we\u0027re still not gonna have more than one user of __pkvm_reprivilege_vcpu()?",
